        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Access",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You're a member of the Vellumis Scholars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You seek to excise the rot from the Gravelands and have made progress to do so. You can cast "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "9e74612a-5951-5a86-b13d-31d1a2609c4c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " as a 6th-rank halcyon spell, and you gain a 6th-rank halcyon spell slot. When you cast your halcyon "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "field of life",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " as a primal spell, any living creatures in the area when you Sustain the spell gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws against curses, diseases, and poisons for 1 round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "afb710eb-b425-5970-a7e0-283a23d92cff"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Special",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " If you have the Halcyon Spellcasting Sage feat, you treat the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "field of life",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " halcyon spell gained from this feat as a signature spell, even though halcyon spells normally can't be signature spells."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
